Package: RepliBayes
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Quantification of Replicability
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ester", "Alongi", email = "ealongi@hsph.harvard.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Gianmarco", "Altoe", role = "aut"),
    person("Giovanni", "Parmigiani", role = "aut"))
Description: A Bayesian hierarchical framework that quantifies the replicability
    of an effect across several studies as posterior probabilities, defined
    relative to a practical-relevance threshold on the scale of the effects
    (epsilon) rather than on p-values. Given study-level data, the package fits
    a hierarchical (partial-pooling) model and an independence-limit model in
    'Stan', and computes empirical, retrospective and prospective replication
    probabilities together with their Monte Carlo standard errors. It also
    provides threshold-free summaries and helpers for prior-sensitivity and
    simulation calibration. Methods are described in Alongi, Altoe and
    Parmigiani, "The Quantification of Replicability".
